---
title: "An Introduction to Data Analysis with R"
subtitle: "Modern workflows with dplyr, gt, and ggplot2"
code-fold: false
format: typst
---
## Basic R Objects and Operations


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# create a vector
x <- 1:10
x <- seq(30, 3, by = -2)
a <- c(66.32, 69.87, 70.12, 90.37, 50.08, 61.20, 65.00, 57.65)
d <- a[1]
a[1] <- 85.34

mean(a)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 68.70375
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
ma <- mean(a)

# read a vector of numbers from a file (assumes files exist)
# x <- scan("data/numbers.txt")
# x2 <- scan("data/number2.txt")

# one can also read number without saving to a file
y <- scan(text = "7  8  9 10 11 12 13 13 14 17 17 45")

# create a matrix
A <- matrix(0, 4, 2)
A <- matrix(1:8, 4, 2)
A
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    5
[2,]    2    6
[3,]    3    7
[4,]    4    8
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
D <- matrix(a, 4, 2, byrow = TRUE)
D <- matrix(1:8, 2, 4)
D
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
     [,1] [,2] [,3] [,4]
[1,]    1    3    5    7
[2,]    2    4    6    8
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
# create another matrix with all entry 0
B <- matrix(1:5000, 100, 50)

# assign a number to B
B[2,4] <- 45
head(B[1,]) # view part of the first row
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1]   1 101 201 301 401 501
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
head(B[,1]) # view part of the first column
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 1 2 3 4 5 6
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
B[1,] <- 1:50

# create a list
E <- list(newa = a, newA = A)
# list the names of components
names(E)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] "newa" "newA"
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
# to look at the component of E
E$newA 
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    5
[2,]    2    6
[3,]    3    7
[4,]    4    8
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
E$newa <- 10:17

# create a dataframe
scores <- c(30, 45, 50)
names <- c("Peter", "John", "Alice")
stat245_scores <- data.frame(names, scores)
stat245_scores
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
`````{=html}
